keel-lnmp-19.0 (5) keel; urgency=low

  * Stable 1, the first stable release (handbook docs/releases/stable-1-plan.md).
    The image is built on the stable track: it reads trixie of
    archive.keellinux.org and not trixie-testing. It carries keel 0.23.49.
    The image has no other change.

 -- KeelLinux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000

keel-lnmp-19.0 (4) keel; urgency=low

  * The image carries keel 0.23.42 from trixie-testing. A MariaDB replica
    that the seed built takes the binary log history of its primary. So
    a first primary that took no write during a cut comes back and
    joins again with no reseed (Keel-Linux/keel#202). A join does not
    say that etcd may not run when another step failed
    (Keel-Linux/keel#198).

 -- KeelLinux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0000

keel-lnmp-19.0 (3) keel; urgency=low

  * The pair example declares the node's overlay address in
    database.server.listen. With the loopbacks alone the primary did not
    answer its replica on hw12-br1.
  * The image carries keel 0.23.39 from trixie-testing. A paired replica
    gets the primary's Anubis key by itself (Keel-Linux/common#56). A
    cut MariaDB primary acknowledges no write that the new primary does
    not get (Keel-Linux/keel#186, #195), and keeps no dump thread that
    hangs the server later (Keel-Linux/keel#193). A rejoined or reseeded
    replica takes the VIP again by itself (Keel-Linux/keel#192). etcd
    starts at the third join with no drift (Keel-Linux/keel#188), and
    the VIP overlay waits for etcd with no drift (Keel-Linux/keel#106).

 -- KeelLinux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 07:55:00 +0000

keel-lnmp-19.0 (2) keel; urgency=low

  * The plan names no webmin-phpini: no archive carries it, and the first
